<section class="page-hero"><span class="pub-kicker">Connected operation</span><h1>Your systems remain yours.<br>StockChief connects the work between them.</h1><p>Initial-launch integrations require a supported merchant account and provider qualification. Optional providers not listed here are not included in self-service plans.</p></section>
<section class="integration-groups">
  <article><header><span>SELLING</span><h2>Commerce and point of sale</h2><p>Completed events enter one normalized order and inventory model.</p></header><div class="integration-grid"><div><b>Square</b><span>Completed POS sales, returns, catalog and locations from a merchant-owned account</span><i class="is-sandbox">Requires provider setup</i></div><div><b>WooCommerce</b><span>Orders, products, fulfillment, cancellations and webhooks from the merchant's store</span><i class="is-ready">Merchant-owned store</i></div></div></article>
  <article><header><span>COMMUNICATING</span><h2>Business mailbox</h2><p>Only mapped supplier and customer communication becomes operational work.</p></header><div class="integration-grid"><div><b>Gmail</b><span>OAuth, approved senders, polling/watch and governed sending</span><i class="is-ready">Provider-qualified path</i></div></div></article>
  <article><header><span>SHIPPING</span><h2>Rates, labels and tracking</h2><p>Optional carrier work uses the business's own qualified shipping-provider account. Postage, labels and carrier charges remain on that account.</p></header><div class="integration-grid"><div><b>Merchant-owned provider account</b><span>Rates, labels, voids and tracking only after provider qualification</span><i class="is-sandbox">Account qualification required</i></div></div></article>
  <article><header><span>MONEY</span><h2>Native accounting</h2><p>Inventory, orders, purchasing and receiving feed StockChief's own operational accounting and reports. External accounting sync and merchant payment processing are not included in initial self-service launch.</p></header></article>
  <article><header><span>CUSTOM SYSTEMS</span><h2>Scoped APIs and inbound events</h2><p>A developer can read authorized records and submit canonical inventory commands or signed business events.</p></header><div class="integration-grid"><div><b>StockChief API</b><span>Scoped inventory reads and controlled commands</span><i class="is-ready">Production-capable</i></div><div><b>Inbound events</b><span>Authenticated, deduplicated business events</span><i class="is-ready">Production-capable</i></div><div><b>Unlisted ERP</b><span>Requires a separately certified implementation and contract</span><i class="is-custom">Not plug-and-play</i></div></div></article>
</section>
